│ patch_name               │ trie_safe_reorder                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The original implementation could not pass validation because it corrupted row identity   │
│                          │ and column placement during recursive/threaded processing. In particular,                 │
│                          │ `as_completed()` results were written using completion order rather than the source row   │
│                          │ index, temporary `original_index` values were mixed into recursive column reordering,     │
│                          │ rows were reconstructed from `.values.tolist()` without preserving labels/types, and the  │
│                          │ method finally returned an empty column-ordering list even though rows may have been      │
│                          │ permuted. The recursive merge/split path could also alter schema semantics and did not    │
│                          │ optimize the evaluator's actual serialized character-prefix objective.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This replacement preserves every source row, cell, index, and shape. It constructs a      │
│                          │ bounded set of valid column-order candidates, including original order, global            │
│                          │ frequency-weighted order, and conditional prefix grouping. Candidates are selected using  │
│                          │ the exact lexicographically-adjacent serialized-row LCP objective. It returns             │
│                          │ row-specific column orderings consistent with the output values, supports mixed types and │
│                          │ missing values, respects merged-column adjacency and one-way dependency precedence, and   │
│                          │ avoids evaluator-state access.                                                            │
