│ patch_name               │ trie_safe_reorder                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The original implementation failed validation because it could alter dataframe structure  │
│                          │ and row/cell alignment during recursive reconstruction. In particular, it created         │
│                          │ dataframes from raw `.values.tolist()`, overwrote rows using completion-order futures,    │
│                          │ added and removed an `original_index` column, merged discarded columns back by value, and │
│                          │ finally sorted rows independently of the returned column ordering. This could duplicate,  │
│                          │ misalign, reorder, or lose original values. It also returned an empty column-ordering     │
│                          │ list despite performing per-row column permutations.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement keeps every original cell, row, column, index, and shape intact. It       │
│                          │ normalizes values only for scoring, builds a bounded set of candidate column-order        │
│                          │ strategies, selects the strategy using the actual serialized-string Trie/LCP objective,   │
│                          │ and returns valid per-row column orderings. Column merge groups are treated as contiguous │
│                          │ ordering blocks and one-way dependencies are respected as ordering precedence             │
│                          │ constraints.                                                                              │
