│ patch_description        │ The original implementation failed validation because it mutates the working dataframe,   │
│                          │ adds and later merges an `original_index` column, recursively rebuilds frames without     │
│                          │ preserving row identity, returns an empty `column_orderings` list, and can reorder values │
│                          │ independently of their source columns. The stdout shows execution reached the recursive   │
│                          │ pipeline, but the program provides no valid ordering metadata and contains several        │
│                          │ shape/index-sensitive paths that can lose or misalign values.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This fix replaces the unsafe recursive dataframe mutation with bounded candidate          │
│                          │ construction. It preserves every input value and row, supports mixed types and missing    │
│                          │ values, returns valid per-row column orderings, honors merge/dependency ordering          │
│                          │ constraints, and selects between a stable original order, a global frequency-ranked       │
│                          │ order, and a bounded conditional grouping order using exact serialized-row Trie/LCP       │
│                          │ scoring.                                                                                  │
