│ patch_description        │ The original implementation corrupts row identity and column alignment during recursive   │
│                          │ processing. In particular, `as_completed()` returns futures in completion order, but the  │
│                          │ code writes results using the enumeration index rather than the source row index. This    │
│                          │ can overwrite rows, detach `original_index` from its data, and later merge incorrect      │
│                          │ cells back together. The recursive code also creates unnamed DataFrames, changes column   │
│                          │ structure, relies on attribute access for arbitrary column names, and returns an empty    │
│                          │ column-ordering list despite permuting cells.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The stdout contains only diagnostic prints and no traceback, which is consistent with     │
│                          │ validation rejecting the returned data rather than a simple runtime exception. The        │
│                          │ replacement below keeps every source row and value, uses object dtype for mixed values,   │
│                          │ returns valid per-row column orderings, and chooses between bounded candidate             │
│                          │ column-order constructions using the actual serialized-string Trie/LCP objective. It does │
│                          │ not modify evaluator state or fabricate helper columns.                                   │
